Additional FedRAMP requirements and guidance:
CM-7 (b) Requirement: The service provider shall use Security guidelines (See CM-6) to establish list of prohibited or restricted functions, ports, protocols, and/or services or establishes its own list of prohibited or restricted functions, ports, protocols, and/or services if STIGs or CIS is not available.$cw$, $cw$technical$cw$, $cw$2$cw$, false),
      ($cw$FED-CM-7(1)$cw$, $cw$Periodic Review$cw$, $cw$(a) Review the system [frequency] to identify unnecessary and/or nonsecure functions, ports, protocols, software, and services; and (b) Disable or remove [organization-defined functions, ports, protocols, software, and services within the system deemed to be unnecessary and/or nonsecure].

